# Netlify headers.
#
# The app is a single 840 KB index.html. Home-screen shortcuts on iOS kept
# serving an old copy of it for days, so this used to say no-store — which
# forbids keeping a copy at all and made every single launch re-download the
# whole file. Inside Telegram, where the app is opened and closed constantly,
# that was seconds of staring at a blank screen every time.
#
# no-cache keeps the guarantee without the cost: the browser must revalidate
# before using its copy, so a new deploy still arrives immediately, but an
# unchanged file comes back as a 304 and nothing is downloaded.

/
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache

/version.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache
